7. My answer to the above issues are as under:
 Issue No.1: In the Affirmative.
 Issue No.2 & 3: Partly in the Affirmative.
 Issue No.4: As per final order;
 for the following:
 //REASONS//
 8. Issue No.1 & 2:- It is the specific case of the petitioners that on 17-11-2019 at about 3.00 p.m., the deceased K N Bhaskar was met with an accident due to rash and negligent driving of offending Mini Lorry by its driver and due to said accident deceased sustained grievous injuries and succumbed to death on the way to the hospital.
 SCCH-9 8 MVC.No.1409/2020  9.

The respondent No.1 & 3 are jointly and severally liable to pay the compensation to the petitioners and respondent No.3 being insurer primarily liable to deposit the said compensation amount within a period of one month from the date of award.
The apportionment of the compensation is as under;
1st petitioner is entitled for 70% 2nd petitioner is entitled for 30%

